[{:db/id "a4110b4e-1a2c-578a-8eae-e4ee8ea9f987" :answer/id #uuid "a4110b4e-1a2c-578a-8eae-e4ee8ea9f987" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "580d3caf-8d8c-5d43-990c-bd6328480355" :answer-field/id #uuid "580d3caf-8d8c-5d43-990c-bd6328480355" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["a4110b4e-1a2c-578a-8eae-e4ee8ea9f987"] :answer-field/correct "a4110b4e-1a2c-578a-8eae-e4ee8ea9f987" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "773eaa1c-93aa-5388-970f-8375245372c9" :question/id #uuid "773eaa1c-93aa-5388-970f-8375245372c9" :question/problem "If $c=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 3k \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],$ $d=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ and $c⊥d,$ then $k=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $c⊥d$ ($c$ and $d$ are perpendicular) if and only if $c\\cdot d=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & ={c}_{x}\\cdot {d}_{x}+{c}_{y}\\cdot {d}_{y}+{c}_{z}\\cdot {d}_{z} \\\\  & =k\\cdot (-3)+3k\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-3k+6k-8 \\\\  & =3k-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot d & =0 \\\\ 3k-8 & =0 \\\\ k & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["580d3caf-8d8c-5d43-990c-bd6328480355"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "5e52e799-9a4a-574e-8348-452560e7951d" :answer/id #uuid "5e52e799-9a4a-574e-8348-452560e7951d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5d488039-835c-51f7-98f3-a614ceeaa760" :answer/id #uuid "5d488039-835c-51f7-98f3-a614ceeaa760" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4ad8e45f-0ef5-5613-af41-2fd293933b76" :answer/id #uuid "4ad8e45f-0ef5-5613-af41-2fd293933b76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "30d15905-64e8-5d18-af76-8acc9e5d07c0" :answer/id #uuid "30d15905-64e8-5d18-af76-8acc9e5d07c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "53d58eb0-0d8f-5cbb-9b43-03bddd83341c" :answer/id #uuid "53d58eb0-0d8f-5cbb-9b43-03bddd83341c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "34df9243-805f-538d-a45b-1fa7022afbc3" :answer-field/id #uuid "34df9243-805f-538d-a45b-1fa7022afbc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["5e52e799-9a4a-574e-8348-452560e7951d" "5d488039-835c-51f7-98f3-a614ceeaa760" "4ad8e45f-0ef5-5613-af41-2fd293933b76" "30d15905-64e8-5d18-af76-8acc9e5d07c0" "53d58eb0-0d8f-5cbb-9b43-03bddd83341c"] :answer-field/correct "53d58eb0-0d8f-5cbb-9b43-03bddd83341c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "0dfb24ed-71db-576c-87d7-7b45fd0ad875" :question/id #uuid "0dfb24ed-71db-576c-87d7-7b45fd0ad875" :question/problem "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ {r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r>0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & ={r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot {r}^{2}+(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-2{r}^{2}-6 \\\\  & =2{r}^{2}-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2}-6 & =0 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =3 \\\\ r & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that $r>0.$ Therefore, $r=\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["34df9243-805f-538d-a45b-1fa7022afbc3"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "9d1acb72-e017-5d70-8eb9-4fdfdb674352" :answer/id #uuid "9d1acb72-e017-5d70-8eb9-4fdfdb674352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8ca76dfd-af74-5089-be0d-ba18af8c7da4" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca76dfd-af74-5089-be0d-ba18af8c7da4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["9d1acb72-e017-5d70-8eb9-4fdfdb674352"] :answer-field/correct "9d1acb72-e017-5d70-8eb9-4fdfdb674352" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "e46cbde8-81fd-5138-9b25-b9d9d745ebf8" :question/id #uuid "e46cbde8-81fd-5138-9b25-b9d9d745ebf8" :question/problem "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}4{r}^{2} \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3{r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$\n\n$r=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot 3{r}^{2}+(-9)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =16{r}^{2}-12{r}^{2}-18 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["8ca76dfd-af74-5089-be0d-ba18af8c7da4"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "9b27be4c-f581-5458-a959-2633136524b3" :answer/id #uuid "9b27be4c-f581-5458-a959-2633136524b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7ff7f755-1ffc-5fd4-8059-46a3459e8c06" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ff7f755-1ffc-5fd4-8059-46a3459e8c06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["9b27be4c-f581-5458-a959-2633136524b3"] :answer-field/correct "9b27be4c-f581-5458-a959-2633136524b3" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d00137d5-07f7-5c87-9146-2b0f0101752e" :question/id #uuid "d00137d5-07f7-5c87-9146-2b0f0101752e" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨{x}^{2},-1⟩$ and $b=⟨2,2⟩.$ If $a⊥b$ and $x<0,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We know that $a⊥b$ ($a$ and $b$ are perpendicular) if and only if $a\\cdot b=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $x<0.$ Therefore, $x=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["7ff7f755-1ffc-5fd4-8059-46a3459e8c06"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "cf664727-ae67-5808-8037-46c3d58535a4" :answer/id #uuid "cf664727-ae67-5808-8037-46c3d58535a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8c9d1a62-29c0-5978-a42e-05d68ed3f2c6" :answer/id #uuid "8c9d1a62-29c0-5978-a42e-05d68ed3f2c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b6def8f7-fa98-5672-a10e-3350a588cd82" :answer/id #uuid "b6def8f7-fa98-5672-a10e-3350a588cd82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "31546151-ec15-571b-a3a0-a043f97c6ce6" :answer/id #uuid "31546151-ec15-571b-a3a0-a043f97c6ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "02e71aa6-0dd2-528b-82f1-c11f714a943c" :answer/id #uuid "02e71aa6-0dd2-528b-82f1-c11f714a943c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e7fa0ba8-9797-51f1-a1a3-612a76531ff7" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7fa0ba8-9797-51f1-a1a3-612a76531ff7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["cf664727-ae67-5808-8037-46c3d58535a4" "8c9d1a62-29c0-5978-a42e-05d68ed3f2c6" "b6def8f7-fa98-5672-a10e-3350a588cd82" "31546151-ec15-571b-a3a0-a043f97c6ce6" "02e71aa6-0dd2-528b-82f1-c11f714a943c"] :answer-field/correct "8c9d1a62-29c0-5978-a42e-05d68ed3f2c6" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "38cba23b-122c-5771-b6e6-8755391889ee" :question/id #uuid "38cba23b-122c-5771-b6e6-8755391889ee" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $u⊥v$ and $a<0$, find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $u⊥v$ ($u$ and $v$ are perpendicular) if and only if $u\\cdot v=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{x}\\cdot {v}_{x}+{u}_{y}\\cdot {v}_{y}+{u}_{z}\\cdot {v}_{z} \\\\  & =a\\cdot a+2\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =10 \\\\ a & =\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $a<0.$ Therefore, $a=-\\sqrt{10}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["e7fa0ba8-9797-51f1-a1a3-612a76531ff7"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "64b8a2f4-8a4c-594f-b127-67b2ef09e03a" :answer/id #uuid "64b8a2f4-8a4c-594f-b127-67b2ef09e03a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{24}{5}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9db5fe94-6940-5997-81bf-5f9c1b0e4a07" :answer/id #uuid "9db5fe94-6940-5997-81bf-5f9c1b0e4a07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "db36b01b-c74b-5c77-9f0e-c9e4710cea66" :answer/id #uuid "db36b01b-c74b-5c77-9f0e-c9e4710cea66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "63819dbc-3f41-5891-90a4-cfb3d79f6d2c" :answer/id #uuid "63819dbc-3f41-5891-90a4-cfb3d79f6d2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e8d6ae85-eb27-5a4a-b111-5532e22cf397" :answer/id #uuid "e8d6ae85-eb27-5a4a-b111-5532e22cf397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{12}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7ba1b053-f29b-56e3-92de-9c65917d5a48" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ba1b053-f29b-56e3-92de-9c65917d5a48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["64b8a2f4-8a4c-594f-b127-67b2ef09e03a" "9db5fe94-6940-5997-81bf-5f9c1b0e4a07" "db36b01b-c74b-5c77-9f0e-c9e4710cea66" "63819dbc-3f41-5891-90a4-cfb3d79f6d2c" "e8d6ae85-eb27-5a4a-b111-5532e22cf397"] :answer-field/correct "db36b01b-c74b-5c77-9f0e-c9e4710cea66" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "85909f08-7094-52c8-bf85-b4e47bc2b8a0" :question/id #uuid "85909f08-7094-52c8-bf85-b4e47bc2b8a0" :question/problem "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}3{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =3{r}^{2}\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-8)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9{r}^{2}-4{r}^{2}-24 \\\\  & =5{r}^{2}-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 5{r}^{2}-24 & =0 \\\\ 5{r}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{24}{5} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["7ba1b053-f29b-56e3-92de-9c65917d5a48"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "f30e7da8-4149-5bae-bf57-17a518398e8e" :answer/id #uuid "f30e7da8-4149-5bae-bf57-17a518398e8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "07b3972e-c239-511d-a71c-02f341be9035" :answer/id #uuid "07b3972e-c239-511d-a71c-02f341be9035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{15}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2c7913a5-a7e3-5bdd-8171-688ecb016f91" :answer/id #uuid "2c7913a5-a7e3-5bdd-8171-688ecb016f91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2bd291ac-ba38-5d8a-a0e8-3f5f1fe8366e" :answer/id #uuid "2bd291ac-ba38-5d8a-a0e8-3f5f1fe8366e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "99847163-4548-58d7-8f0d-3fe134152ee4" :answer/id #uuid "99847163-4548-58d7-8f0d-3fe134152ee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0dd99b61-9868-53dd-b83f-1601d4f65c22" :answer-field/id #uuid "0dd99b61-9868-53dd-b83f-1601d4f65c22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["f30e7da8-4149-5bae-bf57-17a518398e8e" "07b3972e-c239-511d-a71c-02f341be9035" "2c7913a5-a7e3-5bdd-8171-688ecb016f91" "2bd291ac-ba38-5d8a-a0e8-3f5f1fe8366e" "99847163-4548-58d7-8f0d-3fe134152ee4"] :answer-field/correct "99847163-4548-58d7-8f0d-3fe134152ee4" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7db3af69-69b0-5a51-a3ca-bf5d1a73cdb2" :question/id #uuid "7db3af69-69b0-5a51-a3ca-bf5d1a73cdb2" :question/problem "Let $g=[\\begin{aligned}4{r}^{2} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]$ and $h=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2{r}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Given that $g⊥h$ and $r<0$, find the value of $r.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $g⊥h$ ($g$ and $h$ are perpendicular) if and only if $g\\cdot h=0.$\n\nComputing the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & ={g}_{x}\\cdot {h}_{x}+{g}_{y}\\cdot {h}_{y}+{g}_{z}\\cdot {h}_{z} \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 2{r}^{2}+(-10)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8{r}^{2}-4{r}^{2}-30 \\\\  & =4{r}^{2}-30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g\\cdot h & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2}-30 & =0 \\\\ 4{r}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{15}{2} \\\\ r & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the positive solution since we are told that $r<0.$ Therefore, $r=-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["0dd99b61-9868-53dd-b83f-1601d4f65c22"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "338258b5-5456-514c-8754-93cf8061091f" :answer/id #uuid "338258b5-5456-514c-8754-93cf8061091f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c06c6172-5411-5aa2-9336-178c2ad14341" :answer/id #uuid "c06c6172-5411-5aa2-9336-178c2ad14341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cec53d7c-f38a-5d49-be8a-32db3b6b3e54" :answer/id #uuid "cec53d7c-f38a-5d49-be8a-32db3b6b3e54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "714a3214-aa60-50f0-aade-4841169775f6" :answer/id #uuid "714a3214-aa60-50f0-aade-4841169775f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "38237f4f-5129-5256-b140-edb70815c42b" :answer/id #uuid "38237f4f-5129-5256-b140-edb70815c42b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "14f6fb08-46af-5637-b16c-c9f11df73b8f" :answer-field/id #uuid "14f6fb08-46af-5637-b16c-c9f11df73b8f" :answer-field/key "s